{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/905425-need-some-insight-on-bringing-human-pack-members-into-my-werewolf-pack","id":905425,"title":"Need some insight on bringing human pack members into my werewolf pack.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-01T23:21:17-07:00","id":905425,"title":"Need some insight on bringing human pack members into my werewolf pack.","content":"I've been playing a character who began as Wolf-Blooded (he witnessed something he shouldn't have at a young age). As the story progressed, he was forced into his First Change, and became Werewolf. Recently, he and an NPC (who had been werewolf since the beginning) formed an official pack with a Totem. Also included in this pack is my character's girlfriend, who WAS Wolf-Blooded, and became something else.<br /> <br /> One of the Totem's aspirations for the pack is to have at least 6 members (including the Totem itself) in the pack. While discussing this with my ST, we came up with some obvious problems: No one BUT the other werewolf and the girlfriend know what my character is, and since he's high(ish) Harmony, it makes most sense, thematically, that as few people as possible know about him being a 'monster'. He does, however, have three friends outside of the pack, that have all been heavily involved in supernatural experiences with him before (they once tried exorcising a Fear Spirit with Everclear ('liquid courage'). That was fun.).<br /> <br /> So here's my problem: I very much want to get at least two of these three, if not all three, in the pack, WITHOUT telling them that it is, in fact, a werewolf pack. 'The Pack' book details some packs that are run under covers - a street gang, a corporation - which is all fine and well and good, if my character were, say, in New York rather than northern California, or born into wealth like a Trump or a Hilton to make corporations make sense.<br /> <br /> Any insight on the details, rules, or loopholes on how to get humans into a werewolf pack, without them KNOWING that's what it is, would be much, much appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:34:54-07:00","id":905446,"title":"","content":"Well, the corporation thing works because the pack is a <i>corporation</i>, which means it can be presented as one.<br /> <br /> So, what does your pack actually do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:45:44-07:00","id":905451,"title":"","content":"Try using social maneuvering to Secretly inducte them into Pack. Im sure a close group of friends would count as part of the Pack. After all its a supernatural declaration of allegiance. And while the humans won't know what they are apart of they know they are apart of some group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:03:16-07:00","id":905456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/905425-need-some-insight-on-bringing-human-pack-members-into-my-werewolf-pack?p=905446#post905446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the corporation thing works because the pack is a <i>corporation</i>, which means it can be presented as one.<br /> <br /> So, what does your pack actually do?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, to be honest, the most they've done AS A PACK is silently agree amongst themselves who the Alpha is. This literally happened within our last session, so I've got some time to figure out the details. The focus of their pack, as per the Totem they bonded with, is (summed up) the Hunt. The Totem is very iconic for them in terms of loyalty, dominance (and submission, for those for which that applies within the Pack) and the Hunt. Given this, I'd actually raised the idea of presenting the Pack as sort of a paranormal investigation crew - it would allow the werewolves their time to Hunt Spirits, and the others would be helpful and included, but not necessarily catch on to their REAL motivation for this.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:04:12-07:00","id":905457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/905425-need-some-insight-on-bringing-human-pack-members-into-my-werewolf-pack?p=905451#post905451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try using social maneuvering to Secretly inducte them into Pack. Im sure a close group of friends would count as part of the Pack. After all its a supernatural declaration of allegiance. And while the humans won't know what they are apart of they know they are apart of some group.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hadn't even considered this as an option, but it's absolutely plausible, given that my character has the Snarl of the Predator gift (which lets you Force Doors at a lower penalty equal to their dots in Purity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:07:40-07:00","id":905459,"title":"","content":"Well if they have already tred to deal with spirits why not start up a small detective agency and offer to help people with strange problems. This way they can join, help out and only be told what they need to know. Hell, they may even join the ranks of the strange. <br /> <br /> It also helps your case if they discover you when you have been working together to protect and help people. If they become hunters while working with you it'd still possible for relations to be good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:10:57-07:00","id":905462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/905425-need-some-insight-on-bringing-human-pack-members-into-my-werewolf-pack?p=905459#post905459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if they have already tred to deal with spirits why not start up a small detective agency and offer to help people with strange problems. This way they can join, help out and only be told what they need to know. Hell, they may even join the ranks of the strange.<br /> <br /> It also helps your case if they discover you when you have been working together to protect and help people. If they become hunters while working with you it'd still possible for relations to be good!</div> </div> </div> </div>My ST has very heavily implied that something happens to ALL of the 'main characters'. I have obviously already found out what happened to the girlfriend, and the other werewolf (though this happened 'off camera', before the story even started). So I am obviously under the impression that there's more going on behind the scenes, and have even come to my own conclusion that at least one, if not more than, the remaining 'cast members' become Hunters - either BECAUSE of the Pack, or to help them. So yes, this was most definitely my line of thinking as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T04:05:34-07:00","id":905530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tenebra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/905425-need-some-insight-on-bringing-human-pack-members-into-my-werewolf-pack?p=905457#post905457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I hadn't even considered this as an option, but it's absolutely plausible, given that my character has the Snarl of the Predator gift (which lets you Force Doors at a lower penalty equal to their dots in Purity).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go with forced doors. By its very nature forcing a door is a short term rush to get to do what you want. It often burns more bridges then makes them. <br /> <br /> Simply tell your storyteller you wish to use social maneuvering the achive thid goal &quot;peacefully assimilate friends, 1, 2, &amp; 3 into the pack&quot;. That way it goes more smoothly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T04:23:40-07:00","id":905539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/905425-need-some-insight-on-bringing-human-pack-members-into-my-werewolf-pack?p=905530#post905530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't go with forced doors. By its very nature forcing a door is a short term rush to get to do what you want. It often burns more bridges then makes them.<br /> <br /> Simply tell your storyteller you wish to use social maneuvering the achive thid goal &quot;peacefully assimilate friends, 1, 2, &amp; 3 into the pack&quot;. That way it goes more smoothly.</div> </div> </div> </div>And keep in mind that for something like this, you can probably afford to wait out the time period between rolls if your impression isn't great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T05:57:11-07:00","id":905567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/905425-need-some-insight-on-bringing-human-pack-members-into-my-werewolf-pack?p=905539#post905539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And keep in mind that for something like this, you can probably afford to wait out the time period between rolls if your impression isn't great.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My ST is extremely helpful when I'm running short on ideas. He mentioned the Sympathy merit paired with Snarl would be pretty OP. It's probably a last ditch option, but that Sympathy... that's something I'm investing in for the future, whether it's used in this situation or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:18:32-07:00","id":905576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tenebra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/905425-need-some-insight-on-bringing-human-pack-members-into-my-werewolf-pack?p=905567#post905567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My ST is extremely helpful when I'm running short on ideas. He mentioned the Sympathy merit paired with Snarl would be pretty OP. It's probably a last ditch option, but that Sympathy... that's something I'm investing in for the future, whether it's used in this situation or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. I've modeled jury trials in which opposing councel compete for the collective trust of the jury in extended and contested social maneuvering rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}